>     "text": "Turn rapid spanning tree (RSTP) on or off for switches: lan, switch0,lan or all. It is off on a new switch, where a loop of cables storms. Switches with it on send each other BPDUs, choose a root, and block the ports that would close a loop, so a lab can have spare cables. When a cable in use is cut, a blocked port takes over. A switch with it off passes no BPDU on, so a loop through it still storms, and a port towards it carries after 3 seconds. topology has each port's role and state."
>    },
