<     "text": "List the wiring: every switch with its eight ports, what each port's cable goes to, its link (up, cut, or down while the machine at its end is not ready), its conditions, what it delivered and dropped (by loss, rate or MTU), and what the port carries: a VLAN, or a trunk's VLANs and its native one. A cable between switches is at both its ports. A storming switch has storm: its looped frames in the last second, and what it dropped. Then the NICs in no switch. Port 3 of lan is lan:3."
